\DOC SAFE_META_EXISTS_TAC

\TYPE {SAFE_META_EXISTS_TAC : term list ref -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Strips the leading existential quantifier from the goal's conclusion, replacing
the bound variable by a free variable of the same name (primed as needed to
avoid clashing with names already in use in the goal).

\DESCRIBE
The single argument {freevars : term list ref} is a reference cell holding a
list of terms; it does not appear in the printed goal. Applied to a goal whose
conclusion is {?x1. t}, the tactic yields one subgoal whose conclusion is the
body with the bound variable instantiated to a free variable {x1'}, every
occurrence in the body being renamed accordingly; {x1'} is {x1} itself unless
that name already occurs elsewhere in the goal, in which case a primed variant
is used.
{
       A ?- ?x1. t
   =============================  SAFE_META_EXISTS_TAC freevars
       A ?- t[x1'/x1]
}

\COMMENTS
All observed traces show this single kind of outcome, always on goals whose
conclusion begins with one existential quantifier.

\ENDDOC
